ves alone. Call or visit at set times each day, and ask her niece Patricia to do the same on days when no caregiver is scheduled.","frequency":"Daily"},{"name":"Daily Strovia check-in","detail":"Rate balance, eyes, face, arms and speech, and note when anything started.","frequency":"Once every day"},{"name":"Transport","detail":"Rides to therapy and clinic visits, which are a long way from home. Video visits where the clinic offers them.","frequency":"As scheduled"}],"medications":["Antiplatelet or blood-thinning medicine to help prevent another stroke. Report unusual bruising, nosebleeds or any bleeding","Cholesterol-lowering medicine","Blood pressure medicine: taken at the same time every day, never skipped or stopped without the doctor","Heart medicines for the heart condition on record: taken exactly as prescribed, never skipped or stopped","No diabetes medicine is on record; blood sugar was in the usual range"],"diet":["Low salt (DASH-style) eating: vegetables, fruit, whole grains, lean protein, little processed food","Enough protein and energy to keep strength up. Small, frequent meals if tired. Weigh weekly and report weight loss","Sit fully upright to eat; small bites and unhurried meals","Use thickened fluids or softer foods only if the speech-language therapist advises","She stopped smoking. Keep the home smoke-free"],"followUps":[{"who":"Neurology","when":"Every 4 to 6 weeks in the first 3 months"},{"who":"Cardiology","when":"Within 4 weeks, then as directed, for the heart condition and stroke prevention"},{"who":"Primary care (blood pressure)","when":"Within 2 weeks of any hospital stay, then every 3 months"},{"who":"Pharmacist medicine review","when":"Once, within 4 weeks, because several medicines are involved"},{"who":"Memory and mood check","when":"Ask the doctor about it; changes in thinking and mood are common after a stroke"},{"who":"Vision check","when":"If any change in vision is noticed"}],"additional":["The home is in a rural area. An ambulance can take longer to arrive, so keep the phone and alert pendant within reach and the front light on.","Ms. Whitmore lives alone. Her niece Patricia lives about 20 minutes away and is the first family member to call after the office. Make sure someone can get in quickly in an emergency (key safe or a neighbour with a key).","Watch for confusion, low mood or withdrawal and report changes to the office.","Fatigue is expected. Plan rest between therapy sessions.","Encourage her to do as much as she safely can for herself.","Everyone in the home should know the B.E. F.A.S.T. signs and this plan's emergency steps."],"callOfficeIf":["Any change in symptoms — weakness, numbness, speech or vision that is different from usual but not sudden or severe","A new or worsening symptom flagged by Strovia's daily check-in","A fall, even without injury","Missed or refused medication, or a suspected side effect","Blood pressure or blood sugar readings outside the range set by the care team","Coughing or choking during meals, or a wet-sounding voice after drinking","New swelling, redness or pain in a leg or arm","New confusion, low mood, anxiety or a marked change in sleep or appetite","Skin redness or sores where the person sits or lies","A hospital or emergency visit, new prescription, or any change to this care plan","The regular caregiver cannot attend, or equipment is broken or missing","New swelling of the ankles or legs, new breathlessness, or a very slow or very fast pulse","Unusual bruising, nosebleeds or any bleeding (blood-thinning medicine)","She is eating or drinking much less than usual, or is losing weight"],"call911If":["Balance — sudden loss of balance, dizziness or trouble walking","Eyes — sudden vision loss or double vision","Face — one side of the face drooping","Arms — sudden weakness or numbness in an arm or leg","Speech — slurred speech, confusion, or trouble understanding","Time — note when it started, then call 911 straight away","A sudden, severe headache unlike any before","A seizure, or the person cannot be woken","Chest pain, or difficulty breathing","Choking that does not clear, or a fall with a head injury or suspected broken bone"],"review":"Every 30 days, and after any change"}$json$::jsonb
where not exists (select 1 from patients where full_name = 'Agnes Whitmore');

insert into patient_assignments (patient_id, user_id, is_primary)
select p.id, sa.user_id, true
from patients p cross join staff_accounts sa
where sa.company_id = 'C4XXXXX' and sa.role = 'caregiver' and p.full_name in ('Naomi Fairweather', 'Raymond Castellano', 'Beatrice Calloway', 'Leonard Pruitt', 'Agnes Whitmore')
  and not exists (select 1 from patient_assignments pa where pa.patient_id = p.id and pa.user_id = sa.user_id);
